%erg 0.1
Title: Build a static, stripped erg binary via Makefile flags
Created: 2026-05-29
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-05-29T08:30Z Claude created — split out of 0146 (build change is independent of the guard tests)

--- body ---
## Context

The committed `tickets/erg` is **dynamically linked to libc — by accident**:
the Makefile build sets no `CGO_ENABLED=0`, so cgo defaults on when the build
host has a C compiler. A glibc-dynamic binary fails to load on musl/Alpine and
on older glibc — and this binary is *committed and travels with every clone*,
so the failure lands on whoever pulls the repo. It is also larger than it
needs to be: stripping symbols + DWARF recovers ~31%.

Measured (2026-05-29): `go build` (cgo) 9.1 MB dynamic; `CGO_ENABLED=0` 9.0 MB
static; `CGO_ENABLED=0 -trimpath -ldflags "-s -w"` **6.2 MB and static** —
smaller than today's committed 7.6 MB *and* portable.

## Decision

Add the hardening flags to the Makefile build recipe (single source of truth):
`CGO_ENABLED=0`, `-tags osusergo,netgo` (defensive), `-trimpath`, and `-s -w`
appended to the existing `-ldflags` — on **both** the `build` target
(`build/erg`) and the `update-bootstrap-binary` target (`tickets/erg`). Keep
the existing `-X main.buildDate=… -X main.vcsRevision=…` ldflags intact.

## Kind to forks and the upload flow

Putting the flags in the Makefile — not in a workflow — is what makes this
safe for everyone:

- CI's `rebuild-binary.yml` runs `make update-bootstrap-binary` and re-commits
  `tickets/erg`. With the flags in the recipe, the **uploaded** binary is
  static/stripped automatically — no `.github/workflows` edit needed.
- A **fork** that pushes to its own `main` triggers the same workflow and gets
  the same static binary. Nothing fork-specific to configure.
- Users rebuilding from source (`make build`, `install-erg-binary`) get the
  identical result.

The change is purely additive build flags: it breaks no existing flow, and
static is strictly *more* portable for anyone who downloads or clones (now
runs on musl + old glibc, where the dynamic build silently failed).

## Relevant files

- `Makefile` — `build` and `update-bootstrap-binary` targets only. Factor the
  flags into one variable so the two recipes cannot drift.
- No `.github/workflows` change required (CI already calls `make`).

## Test

- `ldd build/erg` ⇒ `not a dynamic executable` (skip-if-`ldd`-absent; on
  darwin assert cgo-free instead — full static is impossible there).
- built binary size < 10 MB.
- binary still runs: `erg version` and a smoke `erg check tickets/`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Flags live in one Makefile variable, applied to both `build` and
      `update-bootstrap-binary`; the `-X` build-stamp ldflags preserved.
- [ ] `build/erg` and `tickets/erg` are static and ~6.2 MB.
- [ ] `make test` / `make validate` green; bootstrap `tickets/erg` rebuilt and
      committed via the normal flow.

## Notes

- Unblocks 0146's standalone (static-link) and small (size-ceiling) guards —
  0146 is `Blocked-by: 0147` so the build lands before the test that asserts
  it ("build and guard land together", as separate units).
- Orthogonal to cross-arch: still amd64; other arches rebuild from source.
- No UPX (per-invocation decompression hurts the *fast* invariant); `-s -w`,
  not external `strip(1)` (which can mangle Go's pclntab).
